<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAZA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Golden_State_Warriors_Point_Guard_Stephen_Curry_01.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAZE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Golden_State_Warriors_Point_Guard_Stephen_Curry_01.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Golden_State_Warriors_Point_Guard_Stephen_Curry_01.jpg/250px-Golden_State_Warriors_Point_Guard_Stephen_Curry_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Golden_State_Warriors_Point_Guard_Stephen_Curry_01.jpg/500px-Golden_State_Warriors_Point_Guard_Stephen_Curry_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="5184" data-file-height="3456" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAZI"/></a><figcaption id="mwAZM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephen_Curry" title="Stephen Curry" id="mwAZQ">Stephen Curry</a> scored a game-high 29 points for the Warriors in Game 2.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAZU">Curry scored 29 points and Golden State outscored Boston 35–14 in the third quarter to tie the series with a 107–88 win. The Warriors outscored the Celtics 43–14 from late in the second quarter to early in the fourth, transforming a tied game into a blowout.<sup about="#mwt128" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_06052022_35-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_06052022"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_06052022-35" id="mwAZY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZg">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZk">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_Poole" title="Jordan Poole" id="mwAZo">Jordan Poole</a> added 17 points for Golden State, including a 3-point shot from <span about="#mwt127" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAZs" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"39"},"2":{"wt":"ft"}},"i":0}}]}'>39 feet (12</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt127"> </span><span about="#mwt127">m)</span>, just past midcourt, with only seconds left in the third quarter, giving them a 23-point lead.<sup about="#mwt129" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_06052022_35-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_06052022"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_06052022-35" id="mwAZw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZ0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ4">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt132" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ganguli_06052022_36-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ganguli_06052022"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ganguli_06052022-36"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ganguli_06052022-36" id="mwAaA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaI">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaM">]</span></span></a></sup> Boston committed 19 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turnover_(basketball)" title="Turnover (basketball)" id="mwAaQ">turnovers</a>, which the Warriors converted into 33 points.<sup about="#mwt135" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_06052022_35-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_06052022"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ap_06052022-35"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_06052022-35" id="mwAaU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAac">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAag">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAak">Green had nine points, five rebounds, and seven assists for Golden State, but impacted the game with his aggressiveness on defense and physical play. He forced a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jump_ball" title="Jump ball" id="mwAao">jump ball</a> on Horford 13 seconds into the game, and was the primary defender on Brown, holding him to 5-of-17 shooting.<sup about="#mwt138" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cacciola_06062022_37-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cacciola_06062022"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-cacciola_06062022-37"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cacciola_06062022-37" id="mwAas"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAa0">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAa4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt141" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-38" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-38"}}'><a href="#cite_note-38" id="mwAa8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbE">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbI">]</span></span></a></sup> Tatum recovered from his poor shooting in Game 1, scoring 21 points in the first half of Game 2 on 7-of-16 shooting. Brown added 15 points in the first half, but Boston still trailed by two at halftime. In the third quarter, Tatum shot just twice in the third period, even though he played all 12 minutes. Horford scored just two points on four shots in the game after scoring 26 in the opener.<sup about="#mwt142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ganguli_06052022_36-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ganguli_06052022"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ganguli_06052022-36" id="mwAbM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbU">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbY">]</span></span></a></sup> The Celtics made just 37.5% of their shots in the game, scoring their fewest points since December 29, when they were 16–19.<sup about="#mwt143" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cacciola_06062022_37-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cacciola_06062022"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cacciola_06062022-37" id="mwAbc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbk">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAbs">The Warriors' <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andre_Iguodala" title="Andre Iguodala" id="mwAbw">Andre Iguodala</a> missed the game due to inflammation in his right knee.<sup about="#mwt144" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ap_06052022_35-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ap_06052022"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ap_06052022-35" id="mwAb0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAb4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAb8">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcA">]</span></span></a></sup> Teammate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gary_Payton_II" title="Gary Payton II" id="mwAcE">Gary Payton II</a>, who played for the first time since fracturing his elbow one month earlier in the series against Memphis, scored seven points in 25 minutes.<sup about="#mwt147" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-39" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-39"}}'><a href="#cite_note-39" id="mwAcI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcQ">[</span>39<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwAcY" aria-labelledby="Game_3"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Game_3">Game 3</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=2022_NBA_Finals&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Game 3"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
